designing movement is honestly one of the things that gives your game its own feel, so the details will depend on what you're going for — but here's a starting point for moving a Rigidbody in 3D that you can tweak from there ^^

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

public class FirstPersonMovement : MonoBehaviour {
	// Rigidbody component used to move the character
	public Rigidbody rb;

	// Use this function to move the character in first-person mode
	void Update() {
		float horizontal = Input.GetAxis("Horizontal");
		float vertical = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");

		// Calculate new position based on input
		Vector3 newPosition = new Vector3(horizontal, 0, vertical);

		// Set the new position of the character's Rigidbody
		rb.transform.position = newPosition;
	}
}
```

this uses `Input.GetAxis()` to grab horizontal and vertical input, then sets `newPosition` as the character's new position. `rb` is the Rigidbody instance you want to move, `transform` is where the character currently is, and `Update()` runs every frame to keep updating the position, wan~
